From: lfdevs <lfdevs@lfdevs.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 00:50:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] screencast: fall back to memfd without a DRM device

The Anland backend can run with surfaceless EGL and no KWin DrmDevice. When PipeWire is available, opening a window preview starts a screencast stream and testCreateDmaBuf() dereferences the missing device, crashing the compositor.

Skip dma-buf probing when no DRM device is available so screencasting uses the existing memfd fallback instead.
---
 src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp b/src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp
index cb51ca2adf..25f6b0d559 100644
--- a/src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/screencast/screencaststream.cpp
@@ -880,7 +880,7 @@ void ScreenCastStream::setCursorMode(ScreencastV1Interface::CursorMode mode)
 std::optional<ScreenCastDmaBufTextureParams> ScreenCastStream::testCreateDmaBuf(const QSize &size, quint32 format, const ModifierList &modifiers)
 {
     EglBackend *backend = qobject_cast<EglBackend *>(Compositor::self()->backend());
-    if (!backend) {
+    if (!backend || !backend->drmDevice()) {
         return std::nullopt;
     }
 
